# Server-side proof that the round trip really happened.  The screen assertions
# alone would pass even if the MSX never talked to the server at all, which is
# the whole reason this file exists.
#
# These match the server's CURRENT log format.  It used to print per-function
# debug lines (pver(), senddata_oneblock(), the checksum comparison); those
# were removed when the server logging was tidied, so asserting on them made
# this test fail while the round trip was working perfectly.  Keep these
# patterns aligned with what msxpi-server.py actually prints, and prefer lines
# that show the command being RECEIVED and ANSWERED over internal details.
MSXPi Server waiting command: -> VER
Sending version info: MSXPi Server Version
